  "why": "All 60 trials COMPLETED and none FAILED, so the arm read as landed — and not one of them was evaluated by the policy engine. The script passed the BARE tool name 'echo' to `McpClient.call_tool`, whose documented `name` is `<TargetName>___<ToolName>`; the gateway answered every call with a JSON-RPC error reading `Unknown tool: echo` (60x isError=True, severityText ERROR in the gateway's APPLICATION_LOGS for 2026-08-12T02:27:10Z..02:27:32Z), which is a rejection at MCP dispatch BEFORE any policy evaluation. Every policy-engine metric in the window therefore had zero datapoints, and F3-10 published a TRUE it had not measured. See DEV-P4-22.",
